<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kagal Senior</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1949 CE (approx.) · capital Kagal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maratha jagir under Kolhapur held by the Ghatge family, which gave Kolhapur its reforming Maharaja, Shahu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kagal was the seat of the Ghatge family, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> chiefs with a long record of service under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> sultanate and the Maratha kings. By around 1700 they held Kagal as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagir</a>, later divided into senior and junior branches, as feudatories of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kolhapur-state">Kolhapur State</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The chiefs governed a small territory south of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kolhapur-state">Kolhapur</a> under its overlordship. The family was closely tied to the Kolhapur court, and in 1884 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahu-of-kolhapur">Yeshwantrao Ghatge</a>, son of the chief of Kagal Senior, was adopted into the Kolhapur royal house, becoming the reforming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> Shahu.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kagal merged with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kolhapur-state">Kolhapur</a> into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1949 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> in 1960. It is now a town in Kolhapur district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1700 CE – 1949 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.96%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 